,"properties":{"data-source-start-line":23,"data-source-end-line":23},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The version comes from "},{"type":"element","tagName":"a","properties":{"href":"https://github.com/python/cpython/blob/036d309cf542986a39eeba5ca805b2ec7619731d/Include/patchlevel.h#L23","className":["external-link"]},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"patchlevel.h"},{"type":"element","tagName":"span","properties":{"ariaHidden":"true","className":["external-link-icon"]},"children":[]}]},{"type":"text","value":". Source citations are pinned to that commit so this graph remains useful without the ignored local checkout. The installed Lat CLI does not expose the external-source registration command described in the project instructions, so citations use ordinary pinned source links."}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{"data-source-start-line":25,"data-source-end-line":25},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The root "},{"type":"element","tagName":"code","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":".gitignore"}]},{"type":"text","value":" excludes the local "},{"type":"element","tagName":"code","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"/cpython/"}]},{"type":"text","value":" checkout, local build directories, frontend output, and macOS metadata. The packaged browser runtime under "},{"type":"element","tagName":"a","properties":{"href":"/lat.md/code/web/public/runtime/runtime.json/"},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"packaged runtime manifest"}]},{"type":"text","value":" is committed. The reference checkout remains unchanged. Disposable builds add the observation module described in "},{"type":"element","tagName":"a","properties":{"href":"/lat.md/runtime#capture-runtime","className":["wiki-link-segmented"]},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"span","properties":{"className":["wiki-link-context"]},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"runtime#"}]},{"type":"element","tagName":"span","properties":{"className":["wiki-link-leaf"]},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Capture runtime"}]},{"type":"element","tagName":"span","properties":{"className":["wiki-link-ref-count"],"ariaLabel":"5 references"},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"5"}]}]},{"type":"text","value":"; performance and undisturbed specialization remain unmeasured."}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"h2","properties":{"id":"comparison-boundary","data-source-start-line":27,"data-source-end-line":27},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Comparison boundary"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{"data-source-start-line":29,"data-source-end-line":29},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The proposed modes are the adaptive bytecode interpreter with JIT disabled and the same CPython revision with native JIT enabled. They share the front end, Python semantics, and initial interpreter execution."}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{"data-source-start-line":31,"data-source-end-line":31},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use a conventional GIL-enabled build for the first comparison. In this revision, "},{"type":"element","tagName":"a","properties":{"href":"https://github.com/python/cpython/blob/036d309cf542986a39eeba5ca805b2ec7619731d/Python/optimizer.c#L129","className":["external-link"]},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"_PyOptimizer_Optimize"},{"type":"element","tagName":"span","properties":{"ariaHidden":"true","className":["external-link-icon"]},"children":[]}]},{"type":"text","value":" has a free-threaded conditional that does not take the normal optimization path. Free threading is a separate topic, not a switch to combine casually with the JIT demonstration."}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{"data-source-start-line":33,"data-source-end-line":33},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"element","tagName":"a","properties":{"href":"https://github.com/python/cpython/blob/036d309cf542986a39eeba5ca805b2ec7619731d/Doc/using/configure.rst#L447","className":["external-link"]},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"configure options"},{"type":"element","tagName":"span","properties":{"ariaHidden":"true","className":["external-link-icon"]},"children":[]}]},{"type":"text","value":" distinguish no JIT, enabled native JIT, native JIT disabled by default, and a micro-op interpreter for debugging. The latter is valuable for inspecting traces but must not be labeled native machine-code execution. The tail-call interpreter is also a dispatch implementation, not the JIT."}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{"data-source-start-line":35,"data-source-end-line":35},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"For matched recordings, prefer the same JIT-capable executable in separate processes with "},{"type":"element","tagName":"code","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"PYTHON_JIT=0"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"element","tagName":"code","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"PYTHON_JIT=1"}]},{"type":"text","value":", after checking build support. Record build flags, architecture, input, and revision with every capture. A no-JIT build is another valid baseline but introduces additional build differences."}]}]},"title":"CPython visualization plan","gitTree":null,"tableOfContents":[{"id":"cpython-visualization-plan","title":"CPython visualization plan","depth":1,"errorCount":0,"hasGitChanges":false},{"id":"source-baseline","title":"Source baseline","depth":2,"errorCount":0,"hasGitChanges":false},{"id":"comparison-boundary","title":"Comparison boundary","depth":2,"errorCount":0,"hasGitChanges":false}],"graphNodeIds":{"":"document:cpython.md"},"errors":[],"backReferences":[{"sectionId":"lat.md/cpython#CPython visualization plan","headingId":"cpython-visualization-plan","references":[{"kind":"markdown","sectionId":"lat.md/lat#CPython X-Ray","breadcrumbs":["lat","CPy